  "interface": {
    "construction": "create_agent(AgentConfig::new(Rc<LlmCall>, retained stages, turn_of, tool_of, payload_of, borrowed TurnView)). Ordinary aliases derive Schema output/error; real AgentCommand::Brain/Tool retains precise leaf values. The real opaque consumer uses inference with one domain Conversation annotation, not fourteen caller type annotations.",
    "ownership": "Canonical AgentState/Conversation/MonitoredRun/FanOut/LlmCall/Schema owners; opaque borrowed stage/argument/provider/result/turn/model cause/tool failure/context have no blanket Clone/serde/Send/static. Only retained Args/Command callbacks earn finite cfg lifetime relations. Conditional AgentCommand serialization delegates the actual flat leaf wire.",
    "lifecyclePrerequisite": "Canonical lifecycle is now Rc<Vec<Rc<AgentLifecycleNote>>>. Source stopWhen can retain an existing tool_failed note before transition appends run_ended. New outer array retains that original note, call and cause handle; the genuine E0308 public red and Source witness are preserved. Prior730 helper proof is not relabeled as append-identity proof.",
    "laws": [
      "Pure init invokes no model/loader/schema/rng callbacks. Brain request uses restored current stage/instructions and invokes turnOf before payloadOf.",
      "The actual Source toolOf is invoked twice per new launch: FanOut builds then discards its Cmd, and armLaunch builds the emitted one. Boot bare-tool reissue calls once.",
      "Guards run only after a fully drained tool batch, in maxTurns, elapsed, then predicate order. Empty tool turns can complete all stages even under zero guards.",
      "Transitions migrate legacy usage, clear the old nonempty note outbox once, retain notes appended within the transition, and append run_ended only on the unsettled-to-settled edge.",
      "Success settles the real LlmCall before folding the turn. Terminal failure retains the full typed LlmErr and original opaque cause.",
      "Boot preserves original startedAt and re-seeds the watchdog before the settled guard. Restart resets the source-owned slices and retains the existing brain ledger.",
      "No blanket terminal gate: late brain success/failure updates resilience after cancel; terminal late fail can retain cancelled run phase plus Llm failure; retry deadlines/timers can remain active after cancel."
    ],
    "nativeCancel": "Agent::cancel is a documented hand-driving convenience for the frozen wired agent_cancel reducer fold; no invented Source AgentKnob.cancel mapping."
  },
